=== REASONING ===

Why this design preserves ADR-015 + P1-P10 + the non-AI baseline:

P1 (Provider port):
  Strategy declares an allowedTools whitelist + a PolicyYearInReview
  redaction policy. It does NOT import provider adapters directly; provider
  resolution is handled by the dispatcher via *provider.Registry.For().

P2 (Decorator chain):
  Provider returned by registry.For() is already wrapped by the
  redaction → rate-limit → cost-cap → audit → trace decorator chain
  (assembled at boot in router.go). Handler does not touch the chain.

P3 (Tool port):
  query_year_in_review_context is the ONE allowed tool (whitelist enforced
  by strategy.AllowedTools). Tool input is validated via shared
  ValidateStruct[T]; tool reads via existing DriveSource + ChargeSource
  interfaces (no new SQL, no bypass of typed handlers).

P4 (Strategy/Dispatcher):
  Handler builds dispatch.New(toolReg, prov, denyAllConfirm, maxIters=4)
  and runs the canonical Run() loop. denyAllConfirm rejects any mutating
  tool (defence-in-depth against future strategy edits).

P5 (Decorator chain locked order):
  Inherited unchanged from registry assembly; handler never re-orders.

P6 (Backend guard + frontend gate):
  Backend: r.Post("/analytics/year-in-review/narrate",
                  g.Wrap("yir-narration", yirHandler)).
           guard.Wrap returns 404 BEFORE handler runs in off mode.
  Frontend: AIYearReviewNarration = withAiFeature('yir-narration', InnerSection).
           withAiFeature returns null in off mode (no DOM, no test ID).

P7 (RAG):
  NeedsRAG=false. The strategy works on aggregates via tool, not RAG.
  This is the same call slice 0012 made for digest-narration.

P8 (Eval goldens):
  3 goldens (standard_year, quiet_year, refusal_other_vehicle) +
  3 canned mock-provider replies. Eval harness exit 0.

P9 (Feature registry):
  yir-narration entry: Tier=U, DefaultOn=false, NeedsTools=true,
  NeedsStream=true, all RouteSet fields populated (no nil slices —
  features.CoverageOK() rejects nil).

P10 (Baseline coexistence):
  Template slide deck is mounted unconditionally on /year-review/:year
  via SLIDE_DEFS. AIYearReviewNarration is overlaid above the slide
  counter, returning null in off mode → slide deck is visually unchanged.

ADR-015 invariants:
  I1 default-off:    DefaultOn=false in registry.
  I3 baseline intact: GET /api/v1/analytics/year-review unchanged;
                     SLIDE_DEFS unchanged; YearReviewPage renders the
                     baseline slide deck unconditionally.
  I4 zero egress:    No provider call possible without ai_mode!=off
                     AND yir-narration toggle on (guard.Wrap blocks).
  I5 hidden UI:      withAiFeature returns null in off mode → no test ID,
                     no DOM. Vitest test asserts container is empty.
  I6 404 routes:     Go test asserts /api/v1/ai/.../narrate returns 404
                     in off mode + body does not leak feature metadata.
  I7 per-feature:    Toggle off WITH mode on still hides UI + 404s route.
  I9 redaction:      PolicyYearInReview allows ClassVehicleName only,
                     wired via redactadapter.Wrap in strategy.New().
  I10 type system:   AI surface lives entirely under /api/v1/ai/*; no
                     baseline JSON shape is modified.
  I12 client/bg:     Background job (ai_yir_pregen) is fail-closed —
                     re-checks AIMode + AIFeatureEnabled on every tick.


